75
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.800
Prompts, resources, and tools differ by
control model. A prompt

76
00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:41.600
is a template the user selects. A resource
is context

77
00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:46.400
the application elects to read. A tool is
a function

78
00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:51.200
the model may propose calling. These
labels describe initiation, not

79
00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:56.000
permission. Prompt text can contain
misleading instructions. Resource data can

80
00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.800
be stale, sensitive, or adversarial. Tool
descriptions and results can

81
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:05.600
attempt to influence later decisions.
Discovery and valid schemas do

82
00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:10.400
not make any of them trusted. The host
decides which

83
00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.200
