112
00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:29.375
applied. If a write times out after
transmission, its outcome

113
00:11:29.375 --> 00:11:34.500
is UNKNOWN. The child may have created the
draft while

114
00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:39.625
the response was delayed. Do not replay
automatically. This fixture

115
00:11:39.625 --> 00:11:44.750
places the expired request id in
quarantine, records a matching

116
00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:49.875
late response as quarantined, and prevents
that response from satisfying

117
00:11:49.875 --> 00:11:55.000
a new request. The diagnostic history is
bounded to 64

118
00:11:55.000 --> 00:12:00.125
identifiers and 5,000 milliseconds. An
unrelated response id remains a

119
00:12:00.125 --> 00:12:05.250
fatal protocol error. Reconcile
deliberately through the read-only state

120
00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:10.375
resource, then decide whether policy
permits another attempt. On shutdown,

121
00:12:10.375 --> 00:12:15.500
close stdin and wait 200 milliseconds. If
needed, send SIGTERM

122
00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:20.625
and wait 200 more. Finally send SIGKILL
and wait no

123
00:12:20.625 --> 00:12:25.750
more than 500 milliseconds. Await cleanup
and reject pending requests.

124
00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:30.875
These exact limits teach bounded behavior;
they are not production

125
00:12:30.875 --> 00:12:36.000
timing advice.

